    "knowledge_point": "Calculating Scalar Triple Products Using Its Properties",
    "problem": "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a),$ if $b\\times c=⟨6,-1,3⟩$ and $a=⟨3,5,-4⟩.$",
    "worked_solution": "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨3,5,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6+5\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =18-5-12 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
